WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.753 --> 00:00:05.755
So the story is about

00:00:05.755 --> 00:00:07.298
the rise of David Rowland,

00:00:07.298 --> 00:00:09.801
the son of a scrap metal
dealer from South London

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:13.680
who rose to become the
confidant to Prince Andrew.

00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:16.891
He had acquired this,

00:00:16.891 --> 00:00:19.519
this Luxembourg bank, Kaupthing Bank,

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:22.981
and they proceeded to turn Kaupthing,

00:00:22.981 --> 00:00:26.067
Luxembourg into what they
now called Banque Havilland.

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:27.986
Prince Andrew had become some kind of a

00:00:27.986 --> 00:00:31.614
roving ambassador for the Rowlands.

00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:32.449
You know, with

00:00:32.449 --> 00:00:35.452
their unofficial door opener of Prince Andrew,

00:00:35.452 --> 00:00:38.496
they kind of went around
the world hoovering up

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:41.332
clients from among the ranks

00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:45.462
of the world's sort of worst
kleptocrats and criminals.

00:00:46.921 --> 00:00:51.009
I don't think anyone comes
out well out of this tale.

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:54.804
Prince Andrew certainly
does not come out well.

00:00:54.804 --> 00:00:57.766
You have the Queen's favorite son

00:00:57.766 --> 00:01:02.312
going out and basically
being a glorified salesman

00:01:02.312 --> 00:01:04.397
for this really quite dodgy bank.

00:01:09.652 --> 00:01:12.238
We thought it would be 
absolutely fascinating to

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:15.158
start having a better, more in-depth look

00:01:15.158 --> 00:01:17.452
at what is Banque Havilland?

00:01:17.452 --> 00:01:18.995
Who are the Rowlands?

00:01:18.995 --> 00:01:21.831
And what is their relationship
with Prince Andrew?

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:27.212
So David Rowland had
very humble beginnings.

00:01:27.212 --> 00:01:31.716
He left school at 16. He's
a short guy, barrel-chested.

00:01:31.716 --> 00:01:35.470
He's got to kind of
near-permanent scowl on his face.

00:01:36.346 --> 00:01:38.765
He peppers his speech

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:41.226
with foul expletives.

00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:42.894
He is a rough character,

00:01:43.853 --> 00:01:46.106
who has done very well for himself.

00:01:47.315 --> 00:01:50.652
By the 1990s, he was well-off enough

00:01:50.652 --> 00:01:53.571
to set up a family office,

00:01:53.571 --> 00:01:56.991
and this family office was not
just handling his own money,

00:01:56.991 --> 00:02:00.245
it was almost like a
shadow banking operation.

00:02:00.245 --> 00:02:02.664
They would provide finance loans

00:02:02.664 --> 00:02:04.749
to the types of people who
couldn't otherwise get it

00:02:04.749 --> 00:02:06.084
but they were very wealthy.

00:02:07.168 --> 00:02:08.753
Not many people in the U.K.

00:02:08.753 --> 00:02:11.256
would have heard of him
until probably about

00:02:11.256 --> 00:02:14.384
late 2010s around that sort of time

00:02:14.384 --> 00:02:16.761
when a lot of these stories
started coming about

00:02:16.761 --> 00:02:18.763
about his friendship with Prince Andrew.

00:02:23.226 --> 00:02:26.688
So Prince Andrew is the second son of

00:02:26.688 --> 00:02:29.649
the Queen of England,

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:34.529
and he is by some
reports her favorite son.

00:02:34.529 --> 00:02:38.283
He's never been in any danger
of being any particularly

00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:40.285
close to becoming King or
anything like that, you know

00:02:40.285 --> 00:02:42.787
so his older brother,
Charles is going to be king.

00:02:44.205 --> 00:02:45.999
You know, he didn't go to university.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:47.917
He went straight into the Navy.

00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:51.337
He then became a pilot
and by all accounts,

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.715
served very bravely in the Falklands War

00:02:53.715 --> 00:02:55.091
as a helicopter pilot.

00:02:55.091 --> 00:02:56.718
That's my helicopter flying

00:02:56.718 --> 00:02:57.760
over at the moment

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.263
I think it's almost time I should go,

00:03:01.306 --> 00:03:03.099
somebody is telling me it's time to go.

00:03:03.099 --> 00:03:03.933
But after that,

00:03:03.933 --> 00:03:07.187
once he left the Royal Navy in the 80's

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:11.316
he seemed to have become a
bit of a lost soul.

00:03:11.316 --> 00:03:13.943
He became a kind of magnet for

00:03:13.943 --> 00:03:16.279
somewhat disreputable people.

00:03:17.405 --> 00:03:21.034
Quite how Prince Andrew
and David Rowland got

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:24.495
into a similar orbit
is not entirely clear.

00:03:24.495 --> 00:03:26.956
All we do know is that they did.

00:03:26.956 --> 00:03:30.960
We know that they've been
friends since at least 2005,

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.253
and one of the earliest
photographs we have

00:03:32.253 --> 00:03:36.507
of the two of them together
is Andrew unveiling

00:03:36.507 --> 00:03:40.637
a larger than life size
statue of David Rowland

00:03:40.637 --> 00:03:44.349
on his Guernsey estate.

00:03:44.349 --> 00:03:46.976
And they are an odd pair.

00:03:46.976 --> 00:03:49.187
Obviously David Rowland is a sort of

00:03:49.187 --> 00:03:51.648
working class boy done good.

00:03:51.648 --> 00:03:55.401
Whereas Andrew is a prince
of the realm who was born

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.820
into fabulous wealth and, you know,

00:03:57.820 --> 00:03:59.948
raised in palaces and castles.

00:04:03.326 --> 00:04:05.161
As we go on air, there are crisis talks

00:04:05.161 --> 00:04:07.789
about how to stabilize the banking system.

00:04:08.665 --> 00:04:09.916
- What started in America last year

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:12.168
has now spread to every part of the world.

00:04:12.168 --> 00:04:13.211
Well, we're down 9%...

00:04:13.211 --> 00:04:15.588
What you had was in 2008, 2009,

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:18.925
you had this banking crash,
and if you had some money

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:21.636
and you were pretty sort of,

00:04:21.636 --> 00:04:24.597
risk tolerant, there was an
amazing opportunity there,

00:04:25.473 --> 00:04:26.808
and the Rowlands seized it.

00:04:26.808 --> 00:04:28.893
They absolutely seized this opportunity.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.730
Kaupthing had been one of the big victims

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:34.357
of the financial crisis.

00:04:34.357 --> 00:04:36.442
It was this Icelandic bank that went off

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:38.778
on this massive lending spree.

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:41.990
And it all came to a
juddering halt in 2008.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:44.867
About 30,000 shareholders
were in Kaupthing

00:04:44.867 --> 00:04:46.744
when the bank collapsed.

00:04:46.744 --> 00:04:47.870
David Rowland came in

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:51.457
and he bought the Luxembourg

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:54.002
arm of Kaupthing Bank.

00:04:54.002 --> 00:04:55.670
They were somewhat desperate

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:56.587
to find a buyer.

00:04:56.587 --> 00:05:00.049
The best buyer before the
Rowlands turned up was

00:05:00.049 --> 00:05:03.428
the Libyan Sovereign Wealth Fund.

00:05:03.428 --> 00:05:07.473
So there weren't a lot of takers
for Banque Havilland,

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:11.394
so that's why David Rowland
managed to get it so cheap.

00:05:13.229 --> 00:05:14.397
And they started to proceed

00:05:14.397 --> 00:05:18.234
to turn what the renamed now Banque Havilland

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:20.361
into this private banking business based

00:05:20.361 --> 00:05:23.948
in Luxembourg and going
after the world's wealthy

00:05:23.948 --> 00:05:25.575
as private banks do.

00:05:25.575 --> 00:05:27.952
Private banks are there
to serve the interests

00:05:27.952 --> 00:05:30.163
the wealth of, of wealthy people,

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:34.083
but it had a slightly
different business model

00:05:34.083 --> 00:05:35.376
to most of them.

00:05:35.376 --> 00:05:37.378
So we find that them going off

00:05:37.378 --> 00:05:40.381
on this amazing worldwide jaunt

00:05:40.381 --> 00:05:43.551
to basically bank the world's
dodgiest people.

00:05:43.551 --> 00:05:46.721
You know, we're talking dictators, we're talking

00:05:48.389 --> 00:05:49.390
scammers.

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:52.268
You know, if you had dodgy money

00:05:52.268 --> 00:05:55.396
the Rowlands were seemingly
interested in you,

00:05:55.396 --> 00:05:57.065
and it didn't really seem to be any limits

00:05:57.065 --> 00:05:59.025
to who they'd go after.

00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:00.902
So for instance, you'd see them go

00:06:00.902 --> 00:06:03.363
for the leadership of Azerbaijan,

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:06.532
which is one of the world's
most corrupt countries on earth.

00:06:09.786 --> 00:06:12.997
The Rowlands flew to Azerbaijan

00:06:12.997 --> 00:06:15.166
with Prince Andrew on their private jet

00:06:15.166 --> 00:06:16.876
a number of times to meet

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:19.504
with President Aliyev

00:06:19.504 --> 00:06:21.297
and his family.

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:23.633
Prince Andrew at the time was

00:06:23.633 --> 00:06:26.260
a trade ambassador for the U.K.,

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:30.890
so he had tried to carve
out this role for himself

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:33.059
and the government had
carved out this role for him

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:35.228
as a special trade envoy
for the U.K.

00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:38.398
Ostensibly he was an ambassador for British business

00:06:38.398 --> 00:06:41.984
and with his royal title,
doors could be open

00:06:41.984 --> 00:06:44.821
for him that wouldn't be
open to ordinary mortals.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:49.409
And the Rowlands

00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:51.953
looked to effectively use

00:06:51.953 --> 00:06:56.290
this relationship, this special
place that Prince Andrew had

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:58.835
to basically get to people
that they wouldn't have

00:06:58.835 --> 00:07:00.294
otherwise been able to.

00:07:00.294 --> 00:07:04.173
You know, remember Banque
Havilland is a tiny,

00:07:04.173 --> 00:07:05.174
tiny institution.

00:07:05.174 --> 00:07:06.968
You're only talking probably

00:07:06.968 --> 00:07:09.178
about a billion or so of assets.

00:07:09.178 --> 00:07:11.597
So if you have this small business

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:14.350
and you want to get
into or close to people

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:16.811
with lots of money, you need a special in,

00:07:16.811 --> 00:07:21.023
and it seemed like their
special in was Prince Andrew.

00:07:21.023 --> 00:07:23.693
They quickly build up a relationship

00:07:23.693 --> 00:07:25.361
with Aliyev's family.

00:07:25.361 --> 00:07:27.280
You might not think that
there's anything wrong

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:30.658
with dealing with presidents of countries,

00:07:30.658 --> 00:07:35.121
but at the time that the Rowlands
were visiting with Aliyev,

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:38.249
he had already been accused
by human rights groups

00:07:38.249 --> 00:07:43.045
of torturing opposition
politicians, of jailing journalists,

00:07:43.045 --> 00:07:47.884
of changing the constitution
to make him president for life.

00:07:47.884 --> 00:07:52.472
Leaked U.S. diplomatic cables
described him as a mafia hood

00:07:52.472 --> 00:07:56.559
who ran Azerbaijan in a manner of

00:07:56.559 --> 00:07:59.562
sort of feudalism in Europe in the middle ages.

00:08:01.772 --> 00:08:03.524
Both sides of the
Atlantic in recent years,

00:08:03.524 --> 00:08:05.943
there's been a big crackdown
on money laundering

00:08:05.943 --> 00:08:08.696
and that has made most
banks incredibly wary

00:08:08.696 --> 00:08:10.781
of who they take on as clients.

00:08:10.781 --> 00:08:13.826
But the Rowlands were a
bit different, you know,

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:17.371
with their unofficial
door opener of Prince Andrew

00:08:17.371 --> 00:08:19.165
they kind of went around the world

00:08:19.165 --> 00:08:22.376
hoovering up clients from

00:08:22.376 --> 00:08:25.505
among the ranks of the world's
sort of worst kleptocrats.

00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:29.675
A sort of prize example
of that is Kola Aluko.

00:08:32.929 --> 00:08:36.516
He was a Nigerian oil magnate who

00:08:36.516 --> 00:08:39.685
came to the Rowlands in 2015

00:08:39.685 --> 00:08:42.271
to get a 25 million euro loan.

00:08:45.733 --> 00:08:48.236
Now if the Rowlands had
done a Google search

00:08:48.236 --> 00:08:50.988
on him at the time, they
would have discovered that he,

00:08:50.988 --> 00:08:54.367
he was already under
investigation in Nigeria

00:08:54.367 --> 00:08:58.663
for his part in a massive,
massive fraud there,

00:08:58.663 --> 00:09:00.957
involving bribery and corruption

00:09:00.957 --> 00:09:04.460
and the awarding of oil contracts,

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:07.880
but they loaned him 25 million euros,

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:11.384
and sure enough, within days
of that loan being signed

00:09:11.384 --> 00:09:14.679
the Nigerian, former
Nigerian oil minister

00:09:14.679 --> 00:09:17.598
was arrested for her part in the fraud,

00:09:17.598 --> 00:09:22.019
and the police started
looking for Kola Aluko.

00:09:26.732 --> 00:09:28.484
Arguably the pinnacle

00:09:28.484 --> 00:09:31.362
of David Rowland's social climb

00:09:31.362 --> 00:09:36.367
was the 2018 wedding of
Prince Andrew's daughter,

00:09:36.617 --> 00:09:37.451
Eugenie.

00:09:40.079 --> 00:09:43.583
Here, you have a
granddaughter of the Queen

00:09:43.583 --> 00:09:47.503
marrying a, on national television,

00:09:47.503 --> 00:09:50.423
at  St. George's chapel,

00:09:50.423 --> 00:09:52.925
which is the same place where

00:09:52.925 --> 00:09:56.637
Prince Harry and Meghan
Markle got married, and

00:09:57.597 --> 00:10:01.142
you have all of the great
and the good of the country

00:10:01.142 --> 00:10:04.562
are, are going in there to be seated

00:10:04.562 --> 00:10:07.148
to, to witness this occasion.

00:10:07.148 --> 00:10:10.443
...to join together this
man and this woman...

00:10:10.443 --> 00:10:12.194
You know, he had front row seats

00:10:12.194 --> 00:10:13.029
with his wife.

00:10:13.029 --> 00:10:16.407
They were in the aisle
sitting next to Kate Moss.

00:10:16.407 --> 00:10:18.993
And there you have David Rowland.

00:10:19.869 --> 00:10:22.788
In... less than six decades,

00:10:22.788 --> 00:10:25.958
David Rowland had ascended from being

00:10:25.958 --> 00:10:28.044
the son of a scrap metal dealer, to,

00:10:28.044 --> 00:10:31.505
to rubbing shoulders with royalty.

00:10:31.505 --> 00:10:34.091
But already at that time,

00:10:34.091 --> 00:10:36.385
the legal noose was,

00:10:36.385 --> 00:10:39.221
was tightening around his bank.

00:10:42.808 --> 00:10:45.853
Kola Aluko had, um, defaulted

00:10:45.853 --> 00:10:48.606
on the 25 million euro loan

00:10:48.606 --> 00:10:51.192
that he owed to Banque Havilland,

00:10:51.192 --> 00:10:55.196
and that had led to
the biggest foreclosure

00:10:55.196 --> 00:10:59.158
in New York history on
this condo that he owned,

00:11:00.743 --> 00:11:02.995
and it became tabloid fodder,

00:11:02.995 --> 00:11:05.998
and for the first time
Banque Havilland were linked

00:11:05.998 --> 00:11:08.250
to this

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:11.003
central figure in one of Nigeria's

00:11:11.003 --> 00:11:13.005
biggest ever frauds.

00:11:13.005 --> 00:11:15.633
And that caught the attention

00:11:15.633 --> 00:11:19.261
of the Luxembourg regulators back home,

00:11:19.261 --> 00:11:21.514
who took a look

00:11:21.514 --> 00:11:24.725
at Banque Havilland's dealings with Aluko,

00:11:24.725 --> 00:11:27.603
and really didn't like what they found.

00:11:28.938 --> 00:11:30.898
When they took a deeper look

00:11:30.898 --> 00:11:33.484
into Banque Havilland's clients

00:11:33.484 --> 00:11:37.196
they found that they were also banking

00:11:37.196 --> 00:11:39.573
the daughters of President Aliyev

00:11:39.573 --> 00:11:42.993
and other prominent Azerbaijanis,

00:11:42.993 --> 00:11:44.829
and they found that they'd done so

00:11:44.829 --> 00:11:48.207
with very little due
diligence, in terms of

00:11:48.207 --> 00:11:52.628
background checks into the
source of their wealth.

00:11:55.005 --> 00:12:00.010
It isn't much fun being
Prince Andrew these days

00:12:00.136 --> 00:12:02.763
ever since photographs emerged of him

00:12:02.763 --> 00:12:05.099
with his arm around the
waist of a young girl

00:12:05.099 --> 00:12:08.352
in the entourage of Jeffrey Epstein,

00:12:08.352 --> 00:12:11.480
he has been somewhat toxic.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:15.234
These days he seldom leaves
the confines of Windsor Park

00:12:15.234 --> 00:12:19.113
where he lives in his,
in a nice big house.

00:12:35.921 --> 00:12:40.926
So the bank's old buccaneering
ways are very much behind it.

00:12:41.385 --> 00:12:45.097
And what you have is this
agreement between the two sides

00:12:45.097 --> 00:12:48.225
that Banque Havilland will
lower its risk appetite.

00:12:48.225 --> 00:12:50.519
The problem you then
have obviously is that,

00:12:50.519 --> 00:12:52.521
well if you're just a normal private bank

00:12:52.521 --> 00:12:54.273
trying to go after the same
people everyone else is,

00:12:54.273 --> 00:12:55.775
why would you bank at
Banque Havilland, right?

00:12:55.775 --> 00:12:57.693
Why wouldn't you go to
some other bigger place

00:12:57.693 --> 00:12:58.944
that has more services?

00:12:58.944 --> 00:13:00.321
And the simple answer to that is

00:13:00.321 --> 00:13:02.782
you would go to one of those places,

00:13:02.782 --> 00:13:03.783
most likely.

00:13:03.783 --> 00:13:06.118
In which case Banque
Havilland really doesn't

00:13:06.118 --> 00:13:07.411
have a purpose any longer.

